{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1005","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E2. Median on Segments (General Case Edition)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an integer sequence $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the number of pairs of indices $$$(l, r)$$$ ($$$1 \\le l \\le r \\le n$$$) such that the value of median of $$$a_l, a_{l+1}, \\dots, a_r$$$ is exactly the given number $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The median of a sequence is the value of an element which is in the middle of the sequence after sorting it in non-decreasing order. If the length of the sequence is even, the left of two middle elements is used."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if $$$a=[4, 2, 7, 5]$$$ then its median is $$$4$$$ since after sorting the sequence, it will look like $$$[2, 4, 5, 7]$$$ and the left of two middle elements is equal to $$$4$$$. The median of $$$[7, 1, 2, 9, 6]$$$ equals $$$6$$$ since after sorting, the value $$$6$$$ will be in the middle of the sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Write a program to find the number of pairs of indices $$$(l, r)$$$ ($$$1 \\le l \\le r \\le n$$$) such that the value of median of $$$a_l, a_{l+1}, \\dots, a_r$$$ is exactly the given number $$$m$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le n,m \\le 2\\cdot10^5$$$) — the length of the given sequence and the required value of the median."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains an integer sequence $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le 2\\cdot10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the required number."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 4\n1 4 5 60 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 1\n1 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"15 2\n1 2 3 1 2 3 1 2 3 1 2 3 1 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"97\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, the suitable pairs of indices are: $$$(1, 3)$$$, $$$(1, 4)$$$, $$$(1, 5)$$$, $$$(2, 2)$$$, $$$(2, 3)$$$, $$$(2, 5)$$$, $$$(4, 5)$$$ and $$$(5, 5)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E2","problemCode":"1005E2","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1005/problem/E2"}